Predecessor slice template (0047): mqtt-sse-inspector-explanations
S6. This slice mirrors its shape — both are scope-bound
narrators with deny-all confirm, PolicyDigest redaction, and a
zero-corpus retrieve_*_chunks tool. The only material differences
are:

  - The body carries a third field (vehicle_id) so the LLM is
    pinned to one vehicle's transitions, not the whole fleet.
  - The PolicyDigest Allow set is strictly narrower (only
    ClassVehicleName vs. 0047's ClassVehicleName +
    ClassRoadSegment + ClassPlaceCategory).
  - The Source type allowlist is {fsm_transition,
    signal_history_summary} instead of {broker_status,
    stream_health}.

=== REASONING ===

Why this design preserves ADR-015 and the non-AI baseline:

1. ADR-015 §I1 default-off: the registry entry is created with
   DefaultOn=false. The feature does not opt-in any user
   automatically; ai_mode must be set to 'local' or 'cloud' AND
   the per-feature toggle must be true for any AI byte to leave
   the box.

2. ADR-015 §I3 baseline intact: the StateMachineDebuggerPage
   continues to render the existing transition table, state
   diagram, FSM health panel, and timeline chart from
   /api/v1/fsm/transitions exactly as it did before this slice.
   The AI narrator section is appended below the FSM health
   panel, never replaces any canonical surface, and is wrapped
   in withAiFeature('state-machine-debugger-narrator', …) so
   it returns null in off mode (the surrounding sections render
   exactly as they did pre-slice).

3. ADR-015 §I4 zero egress: in off mode no AI route exists, the
   AI surface is absent from the DOM, useAiStream is not
   instantiated, no fetch is issued.

4. ADR-015 §I5 hidden UI / §I6 404 routes: the FE wrapper
   returns null when useAiEnabled returns false, and the BE
   handler is wrapped with ai.GuardedHandler which returns 404
   when ai_mode='off' OR the per-feature toggle is false.

5. ADR-015 §I7 per-feature: the guard checks the per-feature
   toggle independently of the global mode — even with mode
   'local'/'cloud', the toggle 'state-machine-debugger-narrator'
   must be true for the route to respond and the FE wrapper to
   render. The positive-control test
   (TestStateMachineNarratorAIOffShowsDebuggerOnly's third case)
   proves both halves of the gate by toggling each input
   independently.

6. ADR-015 §I8 propose-only: the narrator's allowed tools are
   read-only (query_fsm_trace returns a typed envelope;
   retrieve_fsm_chunks returns text chunks). The strategy
   never registers any tool that mutates state. The deny-all
   confirm path inherited from F4 trips immediately if the LLM
   ever tries to call a non-allowlisted tool.

7. ADR-015 §I10 type system: the body is parsed with
   json.Decoder + DisallowUnknownFields. Every field is typed
   (int64 vehicle_id, int64 from_unix, int64 to_unix) and
   validated at the boundary (vehicle_id > 0, 0 < from_unix
   < 2100, to_unix > from_unix, to_unix - from_unix <= 24h).
   No interface{}/any escapes the boundary.

8. ADR-015 §I12 client/background: this slice adds no jobs, no
   push kinds, no client storage keys. The only client-side
   resource it introduces is the SSE stream opened by
   useAiStream — which closes on unmount via the hook's
   AbortController cleanup. The service-worker chunk
   'ai-state-machine-debugger-narrator' is reserved for future
   route-split work; nothing in this slice writes to it.

9. P10 baseline coexistence: the page mounts the AI surface as
   an additive section. The selection mechanism is the
   ai_features toggle map (state-machine-debugger-narrator
   true/false) checked at render time via useAiEnabled — there
   is no branching inside business logic. The transition-table
   handler is left entirely untouched.

10. Redaction (F8): every provider call routes through
    PolicyDigest (Allow=[ClassVehicleName]). The car name is
    the only PII class the operator has explicitly chosen to
    expose to the LLM; VINs, lat/long, place names, IPs,
    emails, phone numbers, MAC addresses, and IDs are
    round-tripped through digests before the message reaches
    the provider. The round-trip-required flag is true; the
    response is unredacted back to the canonical names.

11. Tools (F4): only query_fsm_trace + retrieve_fsm_chunks are
    registered for this strategy. query_fsm_trace is bound to
    a (vehicle_id, from_unix, to_unix) scope installed by the
    handler at request entry — its Execute rejects any call
    whose envelope's vehicle_id, from_unix, or to_unix does
    not match the installed scope OR if no scope is installed
    at all. This is the "LLM cannot widen its own window"
    contract; the test
    TestStateMachineDebuggerNarratorQueryFSMTraceRejectsScopeMismatch
    pins this end-to-end.

12. Goldens (F6): three deterministic goldens land:
    typical_steady_trace (long monotone window proving the
    narrator does not invent flaps where there are none),
    typical_flapping_trace (per-edge flap count must be
    surfaced verbatim, no fabrication), and
    refusal_out_of_scope_request (any prompt asking the LLM
    to widen the window, look at a different vehicle, or
    write/edit/delete FSM state must be refused). The eval
    harness runs against the mock provider so the goldens
    are byte-deterministic.

